 "note": [
  "An Ochorus Original for girls aged 9-12 whose English quotes the Berean Standard Bible; every quotation in this French edition is Louis Segond 1910, pasted byte-for-byte by script, with the reference line in the « Enracinés » form (« — Psaumes 121:1-2 », « (BSB) » dropped, Segond numbering, e.g. Psaumes 4:9). Where the English explains a BSB word Segond lacks (surely, overwhelms, in love, expose, faithful, difficult questions), the French explains Segond's own word instead (viens, s'agitent en foule, dans la charité, condamnez-les, aimables, énigmes), so the quotation stays verbatim; Segond's names are used (Tselophchad and Machla, Phœbé, Priscille, Sarepta, Séba, Loïs, Susanne). The introduction's note that the book quotes the BSB is rendered to name Segond. Rows come from two passes: every printed reference (mined where the block carries a verbatim Segond span of 45+ characters), and every quoted French span of 30+ characters that occurs verbatim in exactly one Segond verse.",
  "AI-translated in-session; awaiting native review."
